@node implemented-and-qualified-scope "Implemented and qualified scope"
@{b}Path               | Implementation             | Current evidence         @{ub}
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Control and bulk;  | Supported                  | Existing issue-23        
mass storage       |                            | baseline reports a       
                   |                            | known-good storage       
                   |                            | device; matched 2.9/2.2  
                   |                            | hardware requalification 
                   |                            | is pending               

Persistent         | Supported with             | Host lifecycle/cadence   
interrupt; HID and | event-driven endpoint      | models pass; Sun HID and 
Ethernet status    | reuse                      | AX88772C issue-23        
                   |                            | hardware gates are       
                   |                            | pending                  

Simple ISO IN/OUT  | Supported at explicit or   | Firmware/driver batch and
                   | ASAP frames                | retirement models pass;  
                   |                            | commercial-Poseidon      
                   |                            | hardware gate is pending 

Realtime ISO       | Poseidon                   | UAC1 capture/playback    
IN/OUT; USB Audio  | add/remove/start/stop      | hardware formats,        
                   | handlers implemented       | cadence, and soak are    
                   |                            | unqualified              

MIDIStreaming      | Descriptor-defined bulk    | Concurrent audio/MIDI    
                   | IN/OUT; independent of ISO | hardware gate is pending 
                   | advertisement              |                          

Hot-plug, abort,   | Generation/epoch fenced    | Host race/error models   
timeout, reset     | with exact-once driver     | pass; 100-cycle hardware 
                   | retirement                 | gate is pending          

Speed/topology     | High speed; split full     | Direct low speed is      
                   | speed behind a high-speed  | deliberately             
                   | hub                        | unadvertised;            
                   |                            | single-TT/multi-TT       
                   |                            | hardware rows are pending

Earlier hardware measurements for a high-speed mass-storage stick were
about 4 MB/s write and 3 MB/s read on a Zorro III-capable Amiga. Treat
those as a historical baseline, not a result for this matched release. See
@{b}docs/usb-qualification-matrix.md@{ub} (../docs/usb-qualification-matrix.md) for
the exact evidence and gaps behind every claim.

@{"Contents" link Main}

@endnode

@node where-the-driver-lives "Where the driver lives"
Release packages ship @{b}zzusbhw.device@{ub} inside the Commodore Installer drawer.
The installer copies it to @{b}DEVS:USBHardware/zzusbhw.device@{ub}; for a manual
install, copy @{b}usb-poseidon/zzusbhw.device@{ub} to @{b}DEVS:USBHardware/@{ub} yourself and
then register it with Poseidon.

The ARM-side USB proxy is part of the firmware. Firmware 2.9 and
@{b}zzusbhw.device@{ub} 2.2 are the matched pair for persistent interrupt and ISO.
The driver negotiates protocol capabilities at startup. With older firmware
it falls back to the constrained legacy transport and does not advertise
simple or realtime ISO.

Some firmware images may expose a ROM copy of the hardware driver, but the
filesystem copy in @{b}DEVS:USBHardware/@{ub} is the release package's explicit
installation path. Confirm with AmigaOS @{b}version ... FILE@{ub} that 2.2 is the
copy Poseidon opens.

@{"Contents" link Main}

@endnode

@node registering-the-driver-with-poseidon "Registering the driver with Poseidon"
After @{b}zzusbhw.device@{ub} is in @{b}DEVS:USBHardware/@{ub}, Poseidon may pick it up
during a hardware scan. If it does not appear, add it from Poseidon's
Trident GUI:

1. Launch @{b}Trident@{ub} (Poseidon's configuration GUI - usually in
   @{b}SYS:Prefs/Poseidon@{ub}).

2. Open the @{b}Hardware@{ub} page.

3. Click @{b}Add@{ub} and fill in:

  - @{b}Driver name@{ub}: @{b}zzusbhw.device@{ub}

  - @{b}Unit@{ub}: @{b}0@{ub}

  - Everything else can be left at the defaults.

4. @{b}Save@{ub}, then reboot (or restart Poseidon) so the stack binds the new
   entry.

The ZZ9000 USB ports should now show up as Poseidon USB hardware.

@{"Contents" link Main}

@endnode

@node superseded-driver "Superseded driver"
Older ZZ9000 releases shipped a separate @{b}ZZ9000USBStorage.device@{ub} that spoke
only the mass-storage subset. It is obsolete and @{b}should be removed@{ub} -
@{b}zzusbhw.device@{ub} via Poseidon replaces it and covers every endpoint type
implemented by the matched firmware and driver. The installer prompts to
delete @{b}Devs:ZZ9000USBStorage.device@{ub} when it finds one.

@{"Contents" link Main}

@endnode

@node troubleshooting "Troubleshooting"
@{b}Symptom             | Check                                                @{ub}
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Driver exposes no   | Confirm firmware 2.9 and @{b}zzusbhw.device@{ub} 2.2, then run
ISO capability      | the matched @{b}ZZDiag@{ub}; legacy fallback intentionally    
                    | hides ISO                                            

Device not detected | Capture @{b}ZZDiag@{ub}, Poseidon's @{b}PsdErrorlog@{ub}, Trident      
                    | binding output, VID:PID, speed, hub address/port, and
                    | TT type                                              

Transfer stops or   | Record the last successful action and the            
returns an error    | driver/firmware epochs, counters, queue state,       
                    | schedule bits, and recent events printed by @{b}ZZDiag@{ub}   

Audio product       | Capture raw string-descriptor bytes plus control     
string ends in @{b}?@{ub}    | requested/actual lengths; do not replace Poseidon    
                    | files or patch displayed text                        

Direct low-speed    | Expected for this release; test low/full speed only  
device is absent    | behind a qualified high-speed hub                    

For anything unexpected, please attach the output of Poseidon's @{b}debug log@{ub}
(enable via Trident -> Main -> Debug) when reporting.

@{"Contents" link Main}

@endnode

